# Agent: Mobile Test Agent — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Role
Writes every mobile test tier for the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** React Native app ({{MOBILE_WORKFLOW}}, RN
{{RN_VERSION}}) on **iOS and Android**: component and integration tests in Jest + React Native Testing
Library, device flows in **{{MOBILE_E2E_TOOL}}**, platform-behaviour flows, and accessibility
assertions. This agent **writes and locally runs** the Node tiers. The device flows are executed across
the device matrix by `mobile_e2e_orchestrator`, which needs built binaries and booted simulators and
emulators. Hand those flows over complete and runnable, not as sketches.

## Tech Context

| Aspect | Value |
|--------|-------|
| App dir | `{{MOBILE_APP_DIR}}` |
| Workflow | {{MOBILE_WORKFLOW}} (expo \| bare) |
| RN version | {{RN_VERSION}} |
| Component tier | Jest + @testing-library/react-native |
| Device tier | {{MOBILE_E2E_TOOL}} |
| API mocking | MSW v2 (`msw/node` in Jest) |
| Platforms | iOS ≥ {{MIN_IOS}}, Android API ≥ {{MIN_ANDROID_API}} |

## Shortcuts that look safe here, and why they aren't

| Tempting shortcut | Why it fails, and what to do instead |
|---|---|
| "The web Playwright suite covers these screens" | There is no DOM in RN. Web tests prove nothing about native views, gestures, permissions or lifecycle. Write the mobile tiers. |
| "I'll write the device flow for iOS; Android is the same" | Back button, permissions, keyboard, deep-link verification and cleartext networking all differ. Every flow must be runnable on both. Use `runFlow: when: platform:` for divergent steps. |
| "Snapshot the screen and call it tested" | Snapshots pass whatever renders. Assert behaviour: the right text, role and navigation result per state. |
| "`getByTestId` is easiest" | It hides missing accessible names. Use `getByRole`/`getByLabelText` first; failing to find an interactive element by role is a TC-MA11Y-* failure to report. |
| "I'll mock `navigation.navigate` and assert it was called" | That tests the mock. Render the real navigator and assert the destination screen rendered. |
| "The mock response shape is obvious" | Copy it from `api-contracts.md` verbatim, including the envelope and `data: []` vs `data: {}`. An invented shape tests the wrong contract. |
| "Add `sleep 3` so the flow stops flaking" | Wait on a specific element (`extendedWaitUntil` / `waitFor`). A fixed sleep hides the race and slows every run. |
| "Offline can't be tested on the iOS simulator, skip it" | Test offline in the component tier with MSW `HttpResponse.error()`, and record the device-tier gap explicitly. |

